iv> </div>Yea, I'll have to re-watch it, it's been a while. I wish they'd gone into a bit more details about the beginning of things, and maybe a bit more about ending the original and the transition to the new, but I know they only had so long...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T16:26:24-07:00","id":1517839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1516222#post1516222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still have a soft spot for Vampire The Requiem despite on how certain parts were not well thought like the emotional issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever I started playing Requiem as a kid, we always just went &quot;Fuck it&quot; and never brought up that angle at the gaming tables, but I was eleven years old when I started playing Requiem and our games were a bit weird anyway. Even our early D&amp;D games were very house-ruled so it wasn't a big issue to do the same for the more &quot;meh&quot; parts of Requiem. I actually created a Requiem nostalgia thread over in the VTR forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T06:14:49-07:00","id":1517870,"title":"","content":"It's funny, I've never played Requiem. When it first came out I thought it had some interesting ideas, but just didn't different enough from Masquerade (I kinda thought with most of the NWoD at first, though I loved the Mortal line). But, I like what they did with 2nd edition (from the little I read), but I just never got around to actually playing it. Maybe some day...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T13:41:03-07:00","id":1517901,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of either form of Vampire (as in, I don't like the idea of playing one, not the mechanics), but Requiem seems... better? to me. Less convoluted, fewer preconceptions that directly impact the setting. I like most of Chronicles for that though, if I wanted a pre-written world I'd just go play a video game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T20:43:31-07:00","id":1524377,"title":"","content":"What I've heard over the years is that the *marketing* of NWoD is what in part killed the new franchise. Apparently LARP players bought the books in far larger numbers than previously understood, and with NWoD, WW went out of their way to alienate them by pushing NWoD hard and lambasting them for wanting to stick with oWoD. The LARPers did not buy NWoD, and sales seriously suffered as a result. This is in addition to all of the other factors others have mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T00:45:17-07:00","id":1524379,"title":"","content":"The situation with the relationship between the LARP community and White Wolf was a lot more complicated than that really sums up. There was a massive falling out between White Wolf and the Camarilla fan club (the largest LARP group because of its close ties to the company) that really wasn't about the move to the nWoD games, that had already drove a huge wedge there.<br /> <br /> The nWoD certainly was the last straw in that mess because WW was tired of their &quot;official&quot; fan club that was getting all sorts of perks and access not treating this as a mutual deal that would lead to the Camarilla to promote official products, while the Camarilla didn't want to be shackled to official stuff for their games (understandably). But that bad breakup was a long time coming before that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T09:01:08-07:00","id":1524388,"title":"","content":"Unpopular opinion, but I don't think nWoD killed White Wolf. I think &quot;personal horror&quot; killed White Wolf.<br /> <br /> Or more accurately the whole toxic mindset of &quot;Personal Horror vs. BadWrongFun&quot; and that whole shift began in Revised Edition.<br /> <br /> Contrary to what a lot of V5 fans (and devs) will tell you, the first edition of Vampire was very much &quot;Trenchcoats and Katanas/D&amp;D With Fangs badwrongfun&quot; but it had the whole &quot;Storytelling Game of Personal Horror&quot; schtick as window dressing. That window dressing was largely a marketing gimmick to try and sell this new game to wider audiences. V1 was very much the most D&amp;D-esque of all the editions of Vampire, and 2e was merely a slightly tweaked and expanded upon take on 1e.<br /> <br /> The Humanity meter was less of a way to enforce personal horror and more of a way to copy the Sanity meter from Call of Cthulhu, as Mark Rein-Hagen and Andrew Greenburg were both huge fans of CoC as well as D&amp;D. The &quot;woe is me, I'm a monster!&quot; angsty shit was merely some fluff to justify this mechanic.<br /> <br /> So much of VTM 1st Edition was just taking stuff from other games they liked and reworking them to fit this modern Gothic-Punk milieu, as the core seven clans all roughly correspond to classes from AD&amp;D 1E in addition to corresponding to various pop culture vampiric archetypes.<br /> <br /> Don't believe me? Once you see this list, you can't un-see it.<br /> <br /> Brujah - Fighter<br /> Gangrel - Ranger<br /> Malkavian - Cleric<br /> Nosferatu - Thief<br /> Toreador - Bard<br /> Tremere - Magic-User<br /> Ventrue - Paladin/Cavalier<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st Edition was the edition that had Alien Hunger, Ashes to Ashes, Awakening: Diablerie Mexico, magic items in the Players Guide, and all the weirdness in both Chicago and Milwaukee, to say nothing of the stuff in The Hunters Hunted that everyone always seems to just gloss over (Kyber Crystals, the &quot;Fist of God&quot; merit, Caiaphas Smith, Greek mages consorting with Elvish warlords in NYC, a vampire-hunting Penn Jillette expy, The Children of Osiris)<br /> <br /> All 2nd Edition did was just pick up where 1st Edition left off. And it was the most successful edition of Vampire for the longest time.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until after Andrew Greenburg had left and more importantly, Justin Achilli had risen to prominence within the company that this shift towards so-called &quot;Personal Horror&quot; really got going.<br /> <br /> The VTM metaplot stopped being this weird little thing that pretty much began and ended in the Chicago city limits and instead became this massive overbearing force that policed the setting of anything Achilli didn't like. The whole false dichotomy of &quot;Supers With Fangs BadWrongFun vs. True Gothic-Punk Personal Horror&quot; also really got going under his watch. Achilli was the guy who saw all the early marketing promos for V1 and took it at face value.<br /> <br /> Then with the Revised Editions of the other game lines, they tried forcing personal horror on the game lines that never even had it as a pretense. The edition wars over Mage: The Ascension were infamous for a reason.<br /> <br /> The only game line of the original World of Darkness that was truly about Personal Horror from day one was Wraith: The Oblivion. VTM only had the flimsiest pretense of personal horror as a marketing gimmick to sell their game to goths prior to Revised. Wraith actually walked the walk. And it sold like shit.<br /> <br /> Everyone forgets that most of Wraith's fandom and acclaim is largely in retrospect. In the 90's, Wraith was considered a failure on all levels and it sold like shit. It bombed so badly that it was the only game line to get a hard cancellation before the Time of Judgment. Even goddamned Changeling: The Dreaming sold better than Wraith, as it only got a soft cancellation around 2001 and at least got some sort of closure with its own segment in Time of Judgement.<br /> <br /> The later WW devs and the more toxic elements of the WoD fandom hitched their wagons closely to Justin Achilli's &quot;True Art Gothic-Punk Personal Horror vs. Icky Trenchcoat &amp; Katana Supers With Fangs BadWrongFun&quot; mindset and helped push the false dichotomy and alienated a lot of people as a result.<br /> <br /> <br /> This push for thematic ideological purism reached its nadir with WoD5 and the controversies over that are still raging as I type this post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 10-22-2023, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T00:58:19-07:00","id":1524413,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'll have any trouble not seeing Malkavians as clerics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T01:50:31-07:00","id":1524416,"title":"","content":"I also think you're giving Justin way too much credit here Matt. Justin didn't run the company or something. He was the VtM lead developer. Even where we have public feuding between the late 2e/Revised devs, it was in execution not over-all direction.<br /> <br /> Like, you have an OK general point in all there, but you're hurting yourself by fixating on one person out of dozens, and stretching a lot facts beyond their breaking points to fit into a narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T04:35:24-07:00","id":1524419,"title":"","content":"Yeah I wouldn't blame Justin or any one guy for it. Its more a general trend which has actually got worse as time ground on<br /> . The personal horror angle is a fine way to run a game, the issue is when it becomes the be all and end all. It's like advocating d&amp;d has to stick with explicit medieval high fantasy dungeon crawlers and stuff such as dark sun, ravenloft, planes cape and homebrew settings are 'wrong' and give them derogatory juvenile nicknames like trenchcoats and kattanas.<br /> <br /> Its also worth noting that their mindset on what personal horror is. For example the descent unto true monstrosity of say a friends lasombra who started as a humanitarian/femminist a degenerated into a sabbat path member (power) were she was taking increasingly dangerous decisions because &quot;why isn't anyone stopping me?&quot; by the end is very hard to replicate this ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T07:18:37-07:00","id":1524423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524413#post1524413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'll have any trouble not seeing Malkavians as clerics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Priests (especially specialty priests, of which there were literally hundreds) were so wide open conceptually by the end of 2e that pretty much anything could qualify. It was a kind of proto-CoDzilla. And if you're going with the &quot;Malkavian as Seer&quot; thing, eh, it might look that way if you tilt your head sideways after a few drinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T08:45:59-07:00","id":1524426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524419#post1524419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. The personal horror angle is a fine way to run a game, the issue is when it becomes the be all and end all. It's like advocating d&amp;d has to stick with explicit medieval high fantasy dungeon crawlers and stuff such as dark sun, ravenloft, planes cape and homebrew settings are 'wrong' and give them derogatory juvenile nicknames like trenchcoats and kattanas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that something billed as a detective noir system and setting has to be all about private eyes engaging in sordid investigations amidst the corruption and intrigue of urban decay.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T09:40:29-07:00","id":1524428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524416#post1524416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think you're giving Justin way too much credit here Matt. Justin didn't run the company or something. He was the VtM lead developer. Even where we have public feuding between the late 2e/Revised devs, it was in execution not over-all direction.<br /> <br /> Like, you have an OK general point in all there, but you're hurting yourself by fixating on one person out of dozens, and stretching a lot facts beyond their breaking points to fit into a narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Justin Achilli may have not been the one running the company per se, but he had a LOT of indirect influence within the company and he used the power he did have as the VTM lead developer to its fullest extent. The devs from the tail end of 2e and Revised helped promote a very toxic mindset that sort of took over the fandom and became the base template for a lot of later devs. <br /> <br /> Their psychotic attitude regarding the fans of the older material or the devs from 1e and early 2e was also quite honestly bad. I'm sorry, but I get the feeling that Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand wasn't as hated when it came out compared to how it is now. Like, now I think most people hate it because Achilli and his cronies have been telling us to hate it for the past two-and-a-half decades. <br /> <br /> They were referencing DSOTBH as late as Vampire: The Dark Ages and the book remained in print up until around late 1997/early 1998. So it sold well enough and it had enough fans that it managed to stay in print longer than either edition of Chicago By Night.<br /> <br /> Whenever I talk to older friends of mine who were actually into VTM back in the 90's, they all mentioned loving <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand </i>and that they were genuinely surprised when all of a sudden, it was condemned by White Wolf as &quot;The Worst WoD Book Ever!&quot;<br /> <br /> While Justin Achilli may not have been the sole WW dev that ruined everything, he was the one who was the most adamant and the one who kept coming back and tellingly, the only old WW dev who was heavily involved with the WoD5 stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T10:25:24-07:00","id":1524429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524428#post1524428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Justin Achilli may have not been the one running the company per se, but he had a LOT of indirect influence within the company and he used the power he did have as the VTM lead developer to its fullest extent. The devs from the tail end of 2e and Revised helped promote a very toxic mindset that sort of took over the fandom and became the base template for a lot of later devs.<br /> <br /> Their psychotic attitude regarding the fans of the older material or the devs from 1e and early 2e was also quite honestly bad. I'm sorry, but I get the feeling that Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand wasn't as hated when it came out compared to how it is now. Like, now I think most people hate it because Achilli and his cronies have been telling us to hate it for the past two-and-a-half decades.<br /> <br /> They were referencing DSOTBH as late as Vampire: The Dark Ages and the book remained in print up until around late 1997/early 1998. So it sold well enough and it had enough fans that it managed to stay in print longer than either edition of Chicago By Night.<br /> <br /> Whenever I talk to older friends of mine who were actually into VTM back in the 90's, they all mentioned loving <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand </i>and that they were genuinely surprised when all of a sudden, it was condemned by White Wolf as &quot;The Worst WoD Book Ever!&quot;<br /> <br /> While Justin Achilli may not have been the sole WW dev that ruined everything, he was the one who was the most adamant and the one who kept coming back and tellingly, the only old WW dev who was heavily involved with the WoD5 stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're giving too much power to one guy, without a doubt at this point, and pretty well ignoring the effect that developers and prominent writers like Stew Wilson, Ethan Skemp, Richard Dansky and many more had on World of Darkness, Chronicles of Darkness as New World of Darkness. Exalted, and other projects.<br /> <br /> But also, genre conceits like personal horror and a particular insistence on it doesn't destroy a franchise-hell, in the discussion of why the original White Wolf ended, personal horror was still a prominent and strongly supported element of Chronicles, and Chronicles is not what killed White Wolf. Lots of successful RPG's these days also do it, with far more restriction towards doing anything else.<br /> <br /> But also, and finally, personal horror insistence is the sort of thing that only affects a small slice of the audience. The majority of the audience for RPG's aren't actively concerned with how the game runs, because realistically most people don't get to run or play games and they come to terms with it, and the next majority of people who play the game tend to be the sort of people who don't find the personal horror as something that interferes with gameplay, often because they get how it informs the setting and mechanics but also actually play the game to discover that momentum of play makes it less of a factor than expected. It's really only a certain slice of those who read and expect to play the game but never really do where you get any actual audience where the personal horror becomes a turn off, because they neither have the experience to know how something like personal horror actually affects gameplay (ie, never as much as they think it does) nor the relaxed set of expectations because they have to imagine everything will follow the tone of the books.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, Rose Bailey's Second Edition for Requiem is better than Justin Achilli's First Edition, and yes, a big part of that is that Rose understood how to balance personal horror with style, class, and energy in a way Achilli isn't prone to doing, but that doesn't mean Requiem First Edition had the power to kill White Wolf, because it pretty clearly didn't. Again, primarily what killed White Wolf was the bad deal with CCP followed by Paradox. White Wolf had ambitions and needed help for fulfilling those ambitions, and sadly the people they partnered with were not actually helpful.<br /> <br /> Like your predecessor on this issue, Paulie Romanov/Camilla, you need to understand that the things you do and don't like are primarily matters for yourself, and to divorce them from larger perception and understanding of issues. Just because you don't like personal horror doesn't mean it actually has the power you think it does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T11:05:11-07:00","id":1524430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524429#post1524429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're giving too much power to one guy, without a doubt at this point, and pretty well ignoring the effect that developers and prominent writers like Stew Wilson, Ethan Skemp, Richard Dansky and many more had on World of Darkness, Chronicles of Darkness as New World of Darkness. Exalted, and other projects.<br /> <br /> But also, genre conceits like personal horror and a particular insistence on it doesn't destroy a franchise-hell, in the discussion of why the original White Wolf ended, personal horror was still a prominent and strongly supported element of Chronicles, and Chronicles is not what killed White Wolf. Lots of successful RPG's these days also do it, with far more restriction towards doing anything else.<br /> <br /> But also, and finally, personal horror insistence is the sort of thing that only affects a small slice of the audience. The majority of the audience for RPG's aren't actively concerned with how the game runs, because realistically most people don't get to run or play games and they come to terms with it, and the next majority of people who play the game tend to be the sort of people who don't find the personal horror as something that interferes with gameplay, often because they get how it informs the setting and mechanics but also actually play the game to discover that momentum of play makes it less of a factor than expected. It's really only a certain slice of those who read and expect to play the game but never really do where you get any actual audience where the personal horror becomes a turn off, because they neither have the experience to know how something like personal horror actually affects gameplay (ie, never as much as they think it does) nor the relaxed set of expectations because they have to imagine everything will follow the tone of the books.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, Rose Bailey's Second Edition for Requiem is better than Justin Achilli's First Edition, and yes, a big part of that is that Rose understood how to balance personal horror with style, class, and energy in a way Achilli isn't prone to doing, but that doesn't mean Requiem First Edition had the power to kill White Wolf, because it pretty clearly didn't. Again, primarily what killed White Wolf was the bad deal with CCP followed by Paradox. White Wolf had ambitions and needed help for fulfilling those ambitions, and sadly the people they partnered with were not actually helpful.<br /> <br /> Like your predecessor on this issue, Paulie Romanov/Camilla, you need to understand that the things you do and don't like are primarily matters for yourself, and to divorce them from larger perception and understanding of issues. Just because you don't like personal horror doesn't mean it actually has the power you think it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think personal horror in and of itself killed White Wolf but I do think that this toxic attitude of &quot;Personal Horror vs. Supers With Fangs&quot; that certain devs and more toxic elements of WoD fandom promoted really hurt WW in the long run by alienating large portions of the fanbase and scaring away potential customers.<br /> <br /> Specifically, certain devs promoted this false dichotomy and went out of their way to alienate a lot of the older WoD fanbase and fans of other games. It was less about how the games were designed and more about how a toxic mindset was promoted within corners of the WoD fandom that put a lot of people off.<br /> <br /> That snooty attitude was like dumping a tank full of gasoline onto the already raging trash fire that was the RPG market in the late 2000's, which likely exacerbated everything. RPG's were in a severe recession in the mid-late 2000's (and damn near everything was in a severe recession by the late 2000's) and this was the era of D&amp;D 4e and all that entailed.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that a lot of people who bought the books are the ones who like you mention, bought the games but never got a chance to run or play them for whatever reason. I do play the games and run them too. Fuck, I've been running a weekly one-on-one nWoD 1e game with my husband for the past couple of weeks so I know that the genre conceits aren't as big of a hinderance as it may seem.<br /> <br /> I'm not against personal horror but I am against this bullshit false dichotomy of &quot;True Art Personal Horror vs. Supers With Fangs BadWrongFun&quot; that still gets promoted in certain online circles because that doesn't help anyone and to be honest, I think that mindset encouraged a lot of the bad changes in the WoD5 books.<br /> <br /> But for the people who couldn't get a game going but still bought the books, this attitude from parts of the company and the more toxic elements of the WoD fandom (mainly the online portion of it) was very off-putting.<br /> <br /> nWoD/Chronicles 1e didn't kill White Wolf, the CCP merger did. But I think had it not been for people like Achilli and the attitude they promoted, then maybe they could've weathered the storm that was the late 2000's a bit better.<br /> <br /> Personal Horror didn't kill White Wolf, but pitting a very specific definition of it against all other forms of gameplay and going out of your way to disparage anyone who doesn't fit that definition when they play the game doesn't win you any favors with your customers. We're seeing this worsen with Parawolf and how WoD5 goes out of its way to shit all over the previous editions of the games.<br /> <br /> Achilli wasn't the only one who did that, but he was probably the most vocal and he had the most influence over the flagship game line of the company when that toxic false dichotomy started to really become prominent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 10-23-2023, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T16:49:07-07:00","id":1524513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524430#post1524430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .<br /> <br /> That snooty attitude was like dumping a tank full of gasoline onto the already raging trash fire that was the RPG market in the late 2000's, which likely exacerbated everything. RPG's were in a severe recession in the mid-late 2000's (and damn near everything was in a severe recession by the late 2000's) and this was the era of D&amp;D 4e and all that entailed.. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true; in the late '00's, was when I bought the majority of my NWoD books, as I could find them cheap, on Amazon and at used book-stores. Now, RPG-books seem to be worth more than college text-books. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T10:30:09-07:00","id":1524528,"title":"","content":"Bit of an unrelated note, but is it wrong that I prefer nWoD/CofD 1e over CofD 2e?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, CofD 2e is well-designed but I have a personal preference for 1e, as it's fine just as is and I have the books around in hard copies, which I also prefer. That's why I've been running nWoD 1e with my husband, starting with just the core &quot;blue book&quot; at first but I'm gonna work in some other stuff along the way. I'm gonna start with the zombie rules from Antagonists and then I will start to work his PC into a major splat, probably Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T10:30:46-07:00","id":1524529,"title":"","content":"The cost of living has gone insane in all fronts it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T10:57:04-07:00","id":1524533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524528#post1524528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of an unrelated note, but is it wrong that I prefer nWoD/CofD 1e over CofD 2e?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, CofD 2e is well-designed but I have a personal preference for 1e, as it's fine just as is and I have the books around in hard copies, which I also prefer. That's why I've been running nWoD 1e with my husband, starting with just the core &quot;blue book&quot; at first but I'm gonna work in some other stuff along the way. I'm gonna start with the zombie rules from Antagonists and then I will start to work his PC into a major splat, probably Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>My preference is the opposite (2e always feels more polished imo, though with its own flaws, obviously), but no, it's not wrong. It's just a preference, y'aint hurting anyone with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:37:21-07:00","id":1524543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524533#post1524533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My preference is the opposite (2e always feels more polished imo, though with its own flaws, obviously), but no, it's not wrong. It's just a preference, y'aint hurting anyone with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable and I get why people like 2e a lot, but I honestly just prefer 1e due to a mix of having a preference for physical copies and nostalgia being a hell of a drug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T16:42:20-07:00","id":1524555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524428#post1524428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I get the feeling that Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand wasn't as hated when it came out compared to how it is now. Like, now I think most people hate it because Achilli and his cronies have been telling us to hate it for the past two-and-a-half decades.<br /> <br /> They were referencing DSOTBH as late as Vampire: The Dark Ages and the book remained in print up until around late 1997/early 1998. So it sold well enough and it had enough fans that it managed to stay in print longer than either edition of Chicago By Night.<br /> <br /> Whenever I talk to older friends of mine who were actually into VTM back in the 90's, they all mentioned loving <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand </i>and that they were genuinely surprised when all of a sudden, it was condemned by White Wolf as &quot;The Worst WoD Book Ever!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Semi-funny story. When I first joined the forums back in like late 2002/early 2003, the mere mention of Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand would get any poor soul flamed to hell and back. But, I loved that book, and I wasn't putting up with any of that. So I started pushing back against it and slowly wearing people down from instantly flaming anyone who mentioned it. Eventually, it wasn't a flame worthy topic and people started admitting they liked it.<br /> <br /> Cut to 2016 and we eventually got a V20 Black Hand book!<br /> <br /> Not that I think that book solely exists because of me, but if I hadn't spoke up so much about it, I wonder if the subject would have revisited.<br /> <br /> But like you said, the book was popular, so popular that it even got a 2nd printing. Hated books don't get second printings...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm a DSotBH Fan, so I had to chime in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T09:52:37-07:00","id":1524593,"title":"","content":"There were some okay elements in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand I liked such as the Nagaraja and Old Clan Tzismice lineages and the notion of an older sect playing the Camarilla &amp; Sabbat off of each other to further there own goals. I didn't care for the True Brujah and there Temporis power and the soul eater ideas and most folks would take creative liberties with such things anyway.<br /> <br /> I don't think to many gamers used the Soul Eater subplot in their games at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T20:34:33-07:00","id":1524614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1504895-did-nwod-kill-white-wolf?p=1524593#post1524593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were some okay elements in Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand I liked such as the Nagaraja and Old Clan Tzismice lineages and the notion of an older sect playing the Camarilla &amp; Sabbat off of each other to further there own goals. I didn't care for the True Brujah and there Temporis power and the soul eater ideas and most folks would take creative liberties with such things anyway.<br /> <br /> I don't think to many gamers used the Soul Eater subplot in their games at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in college we ran a game using Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and went full on with the soul eaters and everything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Ch